    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35438" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνεροι</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>those below, those beneath the
				earth,</i> of the dead and the gods below, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέροισιν ἀνάσσων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.188
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				850
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ ἐνέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.61
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεῦ ἐνέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					629
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέρων ἀρωγός,</span>
			i.e. of the murdered Agamemnon, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1391
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔνεροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					387c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Defix.</u>
				99.9
			</span></i>. (Perh. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρα.</span>)</div>
